    "featuredImage": "/passport-with-schengen-visa-stamp-europe-travel.jpg",
    "publishedAt": "2026-01-08T00:00:00+00:00",
    "readTime": "9 min read",
    "content": "## What is a Multiple Entry Schengen Visa?\n\nA multiple entry Schengen visa allows you to enter and exit the Schengen Area multiple times during the visa's validity period. Instead of applying for a new visa each trip, you can travel freely (within the 90/180 day rule).\n\nThis is ideal for frequent travelers, business people, and those with family in Europe.\n\n---\n\n## Types of Multiple Entry Visas\n\n### By Validity Period\n\n| Type | Validity | Typical For |\n|------|----------|-------------|\n| Short-term | 6 months | New applicants |\n| 1 Year | 12 months | Regular travelers |\n| 2 Years | 24 months | Established travel history |\n| 3 Years | 36 months | Frequent travelers |\n| 5 Years | 60 months | Very frequent, long history |\n\n### Entry Rules Still Apply\n\nEven with a 5-year multiple entry visa:\n- Maximum **90 days** in any **180-day period**\n- Cannot work (unless work visa)\n- Cannot reside permanently\n\n**Example:** With a 5-year visa, you could visit Europe 2-3 times per year, staying up to 90 days total in each 180-day rolling period.\n\n---\n\n## Who Gets Multiple Entry Visas?\n\n### Automatic Eligibility (2020 Rules)\n\nThe EU introduced rules for \"cascading\" longer visas:\n\n**First Schengen Visa:**\n- Usually single or double entry\n- Short validity (trip dates only)\n\n**Second Visa (within 3 years):**\n- Eligible for 1-year multiple entry\n- If first visa was used properly\n\n**Third Visa (within 3 years):**\n- Eligible for 2-year multiple entry\n- If previous visas used properly\n\n**Fourth+ Visa (within 3 years):**\n- Eligible for 5-year multiple entry\n- Clean travel history required\n\n---\n\n## How to Request Multiple Entry\n\n### Step 1: Check Your Eligibility\n\n**You're likely eligible if:**\n- Previous Schengen visa(s) used properly\n- Clean immigration record\n- Strong financial standing\n- Genuine reasons for frequent travel\n\n### Step 2: State It Clearly\n\n**In Application Form:**\n- Select \"multiple entries\" requested\n- Indicate desired validity (realistic)\n\n**In Cover Letter:**\n- Explain why you need multiple entry\n- Describe planned future visits\n- Show history of proper visa use\n\n---\n\n## Strategies to Increase Your Chances\n\n### Strategy 1: Build Travel History First\n\n**Start small:**\n- Get single/double entry first\n- Use it exactly as stated\n- Don't overstay even 1 day\n- Exit before visa expires\n\n**Then apply for longer:**\n- Reference previous visa\n- Show you followed all rules\n- Demonstrate genuine travel pattern\n\n### Strategy 2: Demonstrate Ongoing Need\n\n**For Business:**\n- Letter from employer about European work\n- List of European clients/partners\n- Conference schedules\n- Business registration if self-employed\n\n**For Family:**\n- Relationship proof (marriage, birth certificates)\n- Invitation letters from family\n- Photos of previous visits\n\n---\n\n## Ready for Multiple Entry?\n\nOur experts help you build the strongest possible application for multiple entry visas. We analyze your travel history and optimize your documentation.\n\n**Start your application today!**",
